# npm registry mirror

Always use the project npm mirror — never `registry.npmjs.org` directly.

- Registry: `https://registry.npmmirror.com` (set in root `.npmrc`)
- For every `npm install` / `npm ci` / `npm update` / `npm create`, ensure the mirror is active (project `.npmrc` or `--registry=https://registry.npmmirror.com`)
- If a `package-lock.json` still points at `registry.npmjs.org`, rewrite `resolved` URLs to `registry.npmmirror.com` before install, or reinstall with the mirror so lockfile URLs update
- Do not change the user's global `~/.npmrc` unless they explicitly ask
